ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE ACT ON MANAGEMENT, ETC. OF REAL ESTATE DEVELOPMENT PROJECTS

CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on Management, etc. of Real Estate Development Projects and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Scope of Real Estate Development Projects)
(1) "Uses and sizes prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2, subparagraph 1 (a) of the Act on Management, etc. of Real Estate Development Projects (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means buildings with a total floor area of at least 5,000 square meters whose use falls under any of the following:
1. Multi-family housing under subparagraph 2 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
2. Class 1 neighborhood living facilities under subparagraph 3 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
3. Class 2 neighborhood living facilities under subparagraph 4 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
4. Cultural and assembly facilities under subparagraph 5 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
5. Sales facilities under subparagraph 7 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
6. Hospitals under subparagraph 9 (a) of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
7. Facilities for older persons and children under subparagraph 11 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
8. General business facilities under subparagraph 14 (b) of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
9. General lodging facilities and residential lodging facilities under subparagraph 15 (a) of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
10. Tourist accommodation facilities under subparagraph 15 (b) of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
11. Factories under subparagraph 17 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
12. Warehouse facilities under subparagraph 18 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
13. Data centers under subparagraph 24 (e) of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
14. Tourist rest facilities under subparagraph 27 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act.
(2) "Projects prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2, subparagraph 1 (h) of the Act means projects falling under any of the following:
1. Complex transfer center development projects under the National Transport System Efficiency Act;
2. Enterprise city development projects under Article 2, subparagraph 3 of the Special Act on the Development of Enterprise Cities;
3. Downtown convergence special zone development projects under Article 2, subparagraph 2 of the Special Act on the Establishment and Promotion of Downtown Convergence Special Zones;
4. Logistics terminal businesses under Article 2, subparagraph 3 of the Act on the Development and Operation of Logistics Facilities and logistics complex development projects under subparagraph 9 of that Article;
5. Street block housing improvement projects under Article 2, subparagraph 3 (b) of the Act on Special Cases concerning Unoccupied House or Small-Scale Housing Improvement, small-scale reconstruction projects under item (c) of that subparagraph, and small-scale redevelopment projects under item (d) of that subparagraph;
6. Station area development projects under Article 2, subparagraph 2 of the Act on the Development and Use of Station Areas;
7. Regional development projects under Article 2, subparagraph 3 of the Regional Development and Support Act.

CHAPTER II MANAGEMENT OF REAL ESTATE DEVELOPMENT PROJECTS

Article 3 (Reporting of Project Plans for Real Estate Development Projects)
(1) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as project plans, financial conditions, and financing plans for real estate development projects" in the portion other than the subparagraphs of Article 5 (1) of the Act means the following matters:
1. Matters concerning the name, type, composition, etc. of the project implementer;
2. Matters concerning the project plan, such as the type, method, period, and cost of the project;
3. Matters concerning financial conditions and financing plans, such as equity capital and borrowing of funds.
(2) "Special purpose corporations, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5 (1) 3 of the Act means the following companies:
1. An entrusted-management real estate investment company under Article 2, subparagraph 1 (b) of the Real Estate Investment Company Act or a corporate restructuring real estate investment company under item (c) of that subparagraph;
2. An investment company under Article 9 (18) 2 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act, an investment limited company under subparagraph 3 of that paragraph, or an investment purpose company under Article 249-13 of that Act;
3. A project finance investment company under Article 104-31 (1) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.
(3) "Date prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5 (1) 5 of the Act means the date on which the designating authority publicly notifies the designation of the project implementer pursuant to relevant statutes and regulations (where no public notification is made, the date on which notice of designation as the project implementer is given).

Article 4 (Reporting of Cancellation of Real Estate Development Projects)
"Where the project is suspended for reasons prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as bankruptcy of the project implementer" in Article 6 (1) of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where the project is suspended because the corporation that is the project implementer has been dissolved;
2. Where the project is suspended because the project implementer has been declared bankrupt under the Debtor Rehabilitation and Bankruptcy Act;
3. Where the project is suspended because the status of the project implementer has ceased to exist, such as where designation as the project implementer has been revoked pursuant to relevant statutes and regulations.

Article 5 (Reporting on Progress of Real Estate Development Projects, etc.)
(1) A project implementer (including a person acting on behalf of a project implementer pursuant to statutes, regulations, and contracts; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article) shall report to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport on the progress of a real estate development project, including the following matters, within 1 month from the end of each quarter pursuant to Article 7 (1) of the Act: Provided, That this shall not apply where the cancellation, suspension, or completion of the real estate development project has been reported pursuant to Article 6 (1) or 7 (2) of the Act.
1. Matters specified in the subparagraphs of Article 3 (1);
2. Matters concerning authorizations, permissions, approvals, etc. (including matters concerning changes thereto);
3. Matters concerning the commencement of construction;
4. Matters concerning sales.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems it necessary to prevent unsoundness in real estate development projects, the Minister may require a project implementer to report separately on the progress of a real estate development project in addition to the report under paragraph (1).

Article 6 (Designation of Assessment Institutions, etc.)
(1) Pursuant to Article 9 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may designate a person who meets all of the following requirements as an assessment institution:
1. The person shall be a corporation or organization established pursuant to the Civil Act or another Act;
2. The person shall have the organization and specialized personnel necessary to perform duties such as the assessment of the feasibility of real estate development projects (hereinafter referred to as "project feasibility assessment");
3. The person shall meet other criteria determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as matters necessary for project feasibility assessment.
(2) "Where grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree exist, such as an assessment institution conducting an assessment by improper means" in Article 9 (3) of the Act means any of the following cases: Provided, That designation shall be revoked in a case falling under subparagraph 1.
1. Where the institution obtained designation by fraud or other improper means;
2. Where the institution has failed to meet the designation criteria under paragraph (1) for a reasonable period of not more than 60 days determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
3. Where the institution has inadequately performed duties such as project feasibility assessment intentionally or through gross negligence.
(3) Details concerning the methods and procedures for designation of assessment institutions and revocation of their designation, the operation of assessment institutions, etc., other than the matters prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 7 (Scope of Materials Related to Real Estate Development Projects Excluded from Provision)
Information excluded from the scope of information that may be provided pursuant to the proviso of Article 10 (1) of the Act shall be information falling under Article 9 (1) 7 or 8 of the Official Information Disclosure Act among the information under the main clause of Article 10 (1) of the Act.

Article 8 (Establishment and Operation of the Real Estate Development Project Information System)
(1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may produce and manage the following information through the real estate development project information system under Article 11 of the Act:
1. Information on project plans, etc. for real estate development projects under Article 5 (1) of the Act;
2. Information on the cancellation, etc. of real estate development projects under Article 6 (1) of the Act;
3. Information on the progress of real estate development projects under Article 7 (1) of the Act;
4. Information on the completion of construction of real estate development projects under Article 7 (2) of the Act;
5. Information on project feasibility assessments of real estate development projects under Article 9 of the Act;
6. Information on the operation of the Real Estate Development Project Mediation Committee under Article 12 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Mediation Committee");
7. Other information deemed necessary by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport for the management and supervision of real estate development projects.
(2) Matters necessary for the establishment and operation, etc. of the real estate development project information system under Article 11 of the Act, other than those prescribed in paragraph (1), shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

CHAPTER III MEDIATION OF REAL ESTATE DEVELOPMENT PROJECTS

Article 9 (Functions of the Mediation Committee)
"Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12 (1) 3 of the Act means the following matters:
1. Matters concerning land sales contracts, etc. related to real estate development projects;
2. Matters concerning the terms of agreements for the implementation of real estate development projects (including matters concerning the leasing and operation of the property that is the subject of real estate development projects);
3. Matters concerning the details of authorizations, permissions, approvals, etc. for real estate development projects;
4. Other matters deemed necessary by the chairperson of the Mediation Committee for the smooth implementation of real estate development projects, such as changes to project plans.

Article 10 (Exclusion, Challenge, and Recusal of Members of the Mediation Committee)
(1) If a member of the Mediation Committee falls under any of the following subparagraphs, the member shall be excluded from the deliberation and resolution of the Mediation Committee:
1. Where the member or the member's spouse or former spouse is a party to the agenda item concerned (meaning a person who has applied for mediation pursuant to Article 17 (1) of the Act and the counterparty who has been notified pursuant to the former part of paragraph (3) of that Article; hereinafter the same shall apply) or is a joint holder of rights or a joint obligor with a party to that agenda item;
2. Where the member is or was a relative of a party to the agenda item concerned;
3. Where the member has given testimony, made a statement, provided advice, conducted research, performed services, or conducted an appraisal in relation to the agenda item concerned;
4. Where the member or a corporation to which the member belongs is or was an agent of a party to the agenda item concerned;
5. Where the member or a corporation to which the member belongs was involved in the disposition or omission that gave rise to the agenda item concerned.
(2) If a member falls under any of the grounds for exclusion specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) or circumstances exist that make it difficult to expect impartial deliberation and resolution from the member, a party to an agenda item may file a challenge with the Mediation Committee, and the Mediation Committee shall determine by resolution whether to accept the challenge. In such cases, the member against whom the challenge is filed shall not participate in that resolution.
(3) A member shall recuse himself or herself from the deliberation and resolution of the relevant agenda item if the member falls under any of the grounds for exclusion specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) or determines that circumstances exist that make it difficult to expect impartial deliberation from himself or herself.

Article 11 (Establishment and Functions of the Working Committee)
(1) A Working Committee shall be established within the Mediation Committee under Article 16 (1) of the Act.
(2) The Working Committee shall deliberate on the following matters:
1. Preliminary review of matters for which an application for mediation has been received under Article 17 (1) of the Act;
2. Matters delegated by the Mediation Committee;
3. Other matters referred to a meeting of the Working Committee by the chairperson of the Mediation Committee.

Article 12 (Composition of the Working Committee)
(1) The Working Committee shall consist of not more than 20 members, including one chairperson, with consideration given to gender.
(2) The chairperson of the Working Committee shall be a person designated by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport from among senior public officials responsible for duties concerning the management of real estate development projects at the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
(3) Members of the Working Committee shall be appointed or commissioned by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport from among the following persons. In such cases, a majority of the members shall be persons who are not public officials.
1. Public officials at division director level of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, and the Financial Services Commission;
2. Experts with extensive knowledge and experience in fields such as real estate, urban planning, architecture, finance, accounting, and law.
(4) The term of office of members who are not public officials shall be two years, and they may be reappointed for only one consecutive term.
(5) Where a member falls under any of the following subparagraphs, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may dismiss that member:
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform duties for an extended period due to mental or physical infirmity, etc.;
2. Where the member has engaged in misconduct related to duties;
3. Where the member is deemed unsuitable as a member due to neglect of duties, impairment of dignity, or any other reason;
4. Where the member fails to recuse despite falling under any ground for exclusion under Article 10 (1) or despite circumstances being found in which the member cannot be expected to deliberate impartially;
5. Where the member expresses an intention that it is difficult to perform duties.
(6) The term of office of a member newly commissioned due to the resignation of a member who is not a public official or other such reason shall be the remainder of the predecessor's term.
(7) Article 10 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the exclusion, challenge, and recusal of members. In such cases, "Mediation Committee" shall be construed as "Working Committee".
(8) Where the chairperson of the Working Committee is unable to perform duties for an unavoidable reason, a member designated in advance by the chairperson shall act on the chairperson's behalf.

Article 13 (Operation of the Working Committee)
(1) Meetings of the Working Committee shall be convened by its chairperson.
(2) Meetings of the Working Committee shall be convened with a majority of the members in office present, and resolutions shall be adopted with the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present.

Article 14 (Applications for Mediation)
(1) "Special purpose corporations, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 17 (1) 2 of the Act means the following companies:
1. An entrusted-management real estate investment company under Article 2, subparagraph 1 (b) of the Real Estate Investment Company Act or a corporate restructuring real estate investment company under item (c) of that subparagraph;
2. An investment company under Article 9 (18) 2 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act, an investment limited company under subparagraph 3 of that paragraph, or an investment purpose company under Article 249-13 of that Act;
3. A project finance investment company under Article 104-31 (1) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.
(2) "Documents prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 17 (2) of the Act means the following documents:
1. Project contracts and documents concerning the progress of the project;
2. Documents proving facts concerning the matter for which mediation has been requested, such as real estate sale contracts and project agreements;
3. Other documents or materials necessary for mediation.

Article 15 (Notification of Dismissal of Applications, etc.)
Where any of the following applies, the Mediation Committee shall notify the parties, including the grounds therefor:
1. Where an application for mediation has been dismissed under Article 18 (1) of the Act;
2. Where mediation proceedings have been terminated under Article 19 (5) of the Act.

Article 16 (Commencement of Mediation Proceedings, etc.)
(1) Under Article 19 (1) of the Act, the Mediation Committee shall decide whether to commence mediation proceedings within 15 days from the date of receipt of an application for mediation under Article 17 (1) of the Act.
(2) The Mediation Committee shall prepare a mediation proposal within 60 days from the date on which mediation proceedings are commenced under paragraph (1): Provided, That where an unavoidable reason exists, the period may be extended by up to 60 days following a resolution of the Mediation Committee.
(3) Where the Mediation Committee extends the period under the proviso to paragraph (2), it shall notify the parties of the grounds for and period of the extension.
(4) Where the Mediation Committee intends to request each party and interested persons to attend under Article 19 (2) of the Act, it shall give written notice of the grounds for the attendance request, etc. no later than five days before the meeting. In such cases, a party receiving the notice may submit a written opinion in advance if there is an unavoidable reason preventing attendance at the meeting.

Article 17 (Implementation of Mediation Outcomes and Reports on Progress)
A party that has signed, or written its name and affixed its seal to, the mediation document prepared by the Mediation Committee shall, under Article 21 (3) of the Act, report to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport on the progress of implementation of the mediation outcome in accordance with the reporting intervals and reporting dates specified in the mediation document (where no period is specified in the mediation document, within one month from the end of each quarter), until implementation of the mediation outcome is completed.

Article 18 (Allowances, etc.)
Members and relevant experts who attend meetings of the Mediation Committee or the Working Committee may be paid allowances and travel expenses within budgetary limits: Provided, That this shall not apply where a member who is a public official attends a meeting directly related to the member's duties.

Article 19 (Detailed Rules on Operation)
Except as provided in this Decree, matters necessary for the composition and operation, etc. of the Mediation Committee shall be determined by the chairperson of the Mediation Committee following a resolution by the Mediation Committee.

CHAPTER IV SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 20 (Entrustment of Duties)
(1) Pursuant to Article 23 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may designate an institution or corporation equipped with the personnel, equipment, and expertise to perform entrusted duties from among institutions or corporations falling under any of the following subparagraphs and entrust all or part of the duties listed in the subparagraphs of that paragraph to such institution or corporation:
1. A government-funded research institution established pursuant to Article 8 of the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Research Institutions;
2. A public institution under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions;
3. A nonprofit corporation under Article 32 of the Civil Act.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport entrusts duties pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister shall determine and publicly notify the name of the entrusted institution, the details of the entrusted duties and the methods for performing them, and other necessary matters.

Article 21 (Processing of Unique Identifying Information)
The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport (including a person entrusted with the duties of the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport pursuant to Article 23 (1) of the Act) may process data containing resident registration numbers, passport numbers, or alien registration numbers under subparagraph 1, 2, or 4 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act where it is unavoidable for performing the following affairs:
1. Affairs relating to the receipt and management, etc. of reports under Articles 5 through 7 of the Act;
2. Affairs relating to verification, etc. of the contents of reports under Article 8 of the Act;
3. Affairs relating to the establishment and operation of the real estate development project information system under Article 11 of the Act;
4. Affairs relating to verification of grounds for disqualification of members of the Mediation Committee under Article 14 of the Act;
5. Affairs relating to verification of the contents of applications for mediation and documents under Article 17 of the Act;
6. Affairs relating to verification of the contents of materials submitted pursuant to Article 19 of the Act.

Article 22 (Review of Regulations)
The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall review the appropriateness of the following matters every three years from the respective reference dates specified in the following subparagraphs (meaning by the day preceding the corresponding reference date in every third year) and take measures such as improvements:
1. The scope of real estate development projects under Article 2: January 1, 2026;
2. The frequency of reports on progress under Article 5: January 1, 2026.

CHAPTER V PENALTY PROVISIONS

